        "title": "A payoff ratio is not expectancy",
        "text": "A planned +2R target and −1R stop give a nominal payoff ratio of 2. If the target occurs only 25% of the time and every other outcome is exactly −1R, gross expectancy is 0.25 × 2 − 0.75 × 1 = −0.25R. The break-even win rate for these two outcomes is 1 ÷ (2 + 1) ≈ 33.3%. Costs raise it, and real trades also include time exits and gaps that a two-outcome picture leaves out."
